course: dictionary
lesson: 1052
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Boss can mean the person in charge, or it can mean great. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning to use. Read the words around the word, which is its context.
explain: «Keepers tell animals apart by marks, scars, shape and behaviour, which helps them see who is boss.» Here boss means the leader who is in charge of the group. The clue is who is in charge. Put your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: «In Liverpool a big lad told Ben, "Swap you my phone for your bike, it's boss, worth way more."» This boss means brilliant, not a person in charge. The clue is "worth way more". Try "it's brilliant, worth way more" and it fits. In Manchester, "boss" means great too, so a dictionary can settle it if you are not sure.
fact: Boss can be a noun (the person in charge) or a verb (to boss someone around).
fact: To «boss someone around» means to keep telling them what to do in an unkind way.
fact: In video games, a boss is a very strong enemy at the end of a level.
fact: In Liverpool, «boss» means great, as in «it's boss, worth way more».
fact: A good leader asks and shares, rather than bossing people around.
exercise: «Swap you my phone for your bike, it's boss, worth way more.» What does boss mean here? | A strong enemy in a game | Angry | The person in charge at work | *Brilliant
exercise: «Keepers tell animals apart by marks, scars, shape and behaviour, which helps them see who is boss.» What does boss mean here? | *The leader, the one in charge | Great | A strong enemy in a game | Very angry
exercise: In Manchester, "boss" means great. What does it mean in a game when the boss waits at the end of a level? | Someone who gives kind help | *Brilliant | A very strong enemy at the end of a level
test: «Don't boss me around, I can do it myself.» What does boss around mean? | To win a race | To give a kind present | *To keep telling someone what to do in an unkind way
test: In a game, the boss waits at the end of the last level. What is the boss? | *A very strong enemy at the end of a level | A kind leader in a classroom | Someone who keeps telling others what to do | A friend who helps you win
exam: Which meaning of boss fits «Mum's boss asks her to lead the team»? | To keep telling someone what to do | *The person in charge at work | Great | A very strong enemy in a game
